    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12411539/comment/12667994",
          "id": "12667994",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Can't this functionality be achieved via a normal Filter (and\nChainedFilter if you need to AND two Filters together)?  Ie, why\nintroduce a new interface (with the \"match\" method)?\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-01-28T10:55:00.475+0000",
          "updated": "2009-01-28T10:55:00.475+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12411539/comment/12668244",
          "id": "12668244",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=john.wang%40gmail.com",
            "name": "john.wang@gmail.com",
            "key": "john.wang@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "John Wang",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "Filter calculates a DocSet given an IndexReader. Imagine a large index, and the logic to calculate whether it is in the set is non-trivial, so building this DocSet can be expensive.\n\nSo in the case where the driving query produces a very small result set, the validation can be performed only on the small set via the match call. \n\nYes, in terms of functionality, one can do this with a filter, but it is wasteful to perform the validation calculation on the entire index where the candidates to be in the hits set is small.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=john.wang%40gmail.com",
            "name": "john.wang@gmail.com",
            "key": "john.wang@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "John Wang",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2009-01-28T23:59:26.998+0000",
          "updated": "2009-01-28T23:59:26.998+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12411539/comment/12668399",
          "id": "12668399",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "OK, I see.  That is an important difference; I think it makes sense to add this.  Could you add javadocs & a unit test?  Thanks John.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
